# Telegram Mini App decision surface.
#
# Rendered and installed by bin/fm-miniapp-deploy.sh, which substitutes
# __ADDRESS__ and __UPSTREAM__ from local configuration. The template carries no
# hostname and no port, so no installation's concrete address ends up in shared
# material.
#
# This block is deliberately three lines, and each omission is load-bearing:
#
#   - No basic_auth. The access control here is the initData signature check;
#     Telegram's built-in web view cannot serve a password prompt, and a block
#     copied from a neighbour brings one along. That is one of the ways this
#     page shows up as "does not load".
#   - No path list. Enumerating /, /app.js and /answer means the next route the
#     service grows 404s until someone remembers this file. Pass everything
#     through instead.
#   - No content-security-policy here. The service sends its own; a second one
#     applies on top and the stricter of the two wins, which blocks the page's
#     script exactly as an inline <script> block would.
__ADDRESS__ {
	reverse_proxy __UPSTREAM__
}
